{"name":"Honeysuckle","hex":"#e8ed69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Honeysuckle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name.","A suburb of Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The ship of characters Kim and Basil from the video game Omori."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Honeysuckle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honeysuckle","blocks":[{"text":"Honeysuckles are arching shrubs or twining vines in the genus Lonicera of the family Caprifoliaceae. The genus includes 158 species native to northern latitudes in North America, Eurasia, and North Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Lonicera_caprifolium001.jpg/330px-Lonicera_caprifolium001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeysuckle","wikidata":"Q156047"},{"title":"Honeysuckle (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Honeysuckle is a British-bred, Irish-trained Thoroughbred racehorse who competed in National Hunt races. She won seventeen of her nineteen races across five seasons, including two Champion Hurdles, two Mares' Hurdles, three Irish Champion Hurdles and two Punchestown Champion Hurdles. She was trained by Henry de Bromhead and ridden by Rachael Blackmore in all her races under rules. She was retired at the age of nine in 2023 and had her first foal in March 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeysuckle_(horse)","wikidata":"Q92866459"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Honeysuckle-2.jpg/500px-Honeysuckle-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Honeysuckle-2.jpg/1280px-Honeysuckle-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Honeysuckle-2.jpg/500px-Honeysuckle-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Honeysuckle (Lonicera japonica)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoneysuckle-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg/500px-Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg/1280px-Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg/500px-Wild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_%2831658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wild honeysuckle buds in New York","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWild_honeysuckle_Bashakill_(31658).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Honeysuckle-1.jpg/120px-Honeysuckle-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Honeysuckle-1.jpg/250px-Honeysuckle-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Honeysuckle-1.jpg/120px-Honeysuckle-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoneysuckle-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lonicera_ciliosa_13310.JPG/120px-Lonicera_ciliosa_13310.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lonicera_ciliosa_13310.JPG/250px-Lonicera_ciliosa_13310.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x